{"id":97827149,"q":"Q97827149","imdb":"tt12716170","en":"Laila in Haifa","orig":"Laila in Haifa","ar":null,"tag":null,"ov":"","plotEn":"Laila in Haifa (Hebrew title: לילה בחיפה, Layla BeHaifa) is a 2020 Israeli-French comedy-drama film directed by Amos Gitai. It was selected to be shown in the main competition section of the 77th Venice International Film Festival.\nThe events of the film take place over one night in a club in Haifa, Israel. The club Fattoush is the place where people of different background meet, as the director of the film puts it: \"men and women, straight and gay, Jews and Arabs, radical and moderate\".","rd":"2020-09-07","rt":99,"g":[18],"lang":"he","budget":0,"revenue":0,"companies":[],"countries":["FR","IL"],"langs":[],"col":null,"rel":[],"dir":["Amos Gitai"],"prod":["Amos Gitai","Moshe Edri","Leon Edery","Laurent Truchot","Catherine Dussart"],"wri":["Amos Gitai"],"mus":[],"dop":["Éric Gautier"],"cast":[{"n":"Maria Zreik","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Khawla Ibraheem","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Bahira Ablassi","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Naama Preis","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Tsahi Halevi","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Makram J. Khoury","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Makram Khoury","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Hisham Sulliman","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Hisham Suliman","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Tzachi HaLevy","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Hana Laszlo","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Amir Khoury","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Tom Baum","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Andrzej Seweryn","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Andrzej Seweryn","ch":"","p":null},{"n":"Clara Khoury","ch":"","p":null}],"wiki":{"en":"Laila in Haifa","ar":null},"wk":1795623235314,"castOrder":["Maria Zreik","Khawla Ibraheem","Bahira Ablassi","Naama Preis","Tsahi Halevi","Makram J. Khoury"]}